= Computer science and philosophy course of the University of Oxford
{parent=Undergraduate course of the University of Oxford}
{title2=BA, MCompSciPhil}

https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/undergraduate/courses/course-listing/computer-science-and-philosophy[Official course description].

= Year 1 of the computer science and philosophy course of the University of Oxford
{parent=Computer science and philosophy course of the University of Oxford}
{title2=Prelims}

Two shared programming/<algorithms>/proof-systems papers, discrete <mathematics> and <probability>, introduction to philosophy, and philosophical topics in logic and <probability>.

= Year 2 of the computer science and philosophy course of the University of Oxford
{parent=Computer science and philosophy course of the University of Oxford}
{title2=Part A}

<Algorithms> and <data structures>, models of computation, group design practical, and options; philosophy teaching continues.

= Year 3 of the computer science and philosophy course of the University of Oxford
{parent=Computer science and philosophy course of the University of Oxford}
{title2=Part B}

<Computer science> options and philosophy papers, including at least three philosophy examinations.

= Year 4 of the computer science and philosophy course of the University of Oxford
{parent=Computer science and philosophy course of the University of Oxford}
{title2=Part C}

Advanced <computer science> and/or philosophy papers; project or thesis choices follow the joint course rules.

