= MSc in advanced computer science course of the University of Oxford
{parent=Master's course of the University of Oxford}
{c}

https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/graduate/courses/msc-advanced-computer-science[Official course description].

At least six options. The https://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/teaching/MSCinCS/[current teaching list] distinguishes written examinations from mini-projects and sets out the specialist streams. Shared examined modules include <Automata, logic and games course of the University of Oxford>, <Categories, proofs and processes course of the University of Oxford> and <Quantum processes and computation course of the University of Oxford>. Independent supervised project during Trinity term and the summer.

\Include[past-exam-of-the-msc-in-advanced-computer-science-course-of-the-university-of-oxford]

= MSc in advanced computer science (artificial intelligence) course of the University of Oxford
{parent=MSc in advanced computer science course of the University of Oxford}
{c}

https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/graduate/courses/msc-advanced-computer-science[Official course description]. Specialist award/stream within Advanced <Computer Science>; not counted as a separately indexed standalone programme. The specialist menu includes computer vision, geometric deep learning, computational learning theory and foundations of self-programming agents. https://www.cs.ox.ac.uk/teaching/MSCinCS/[Official specialist module lists].

= MSc in advanced computer science (foundations of computer science) course of the University of Oxford
{parent=MSc in advanced computer science course of the University of Oxford}
{c}

