= MSc in statistical science course of the University of Oxford
{parent=Master's course of the University of Oxford}
{c}

https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/graduate/courses/msc-statistical-science[Official course description].

Five core modules: applied <statistics>; foundations of <statistical inference>; statistical programming; computational <statistics>; statistical <machine learning>. Four option units are also required. The central page labels its option examples as 2025–26, so they are not presented here as a guaranteed current list. Compulsory dissertation, with the main work taking place from June to September.

